A: Here is a way to do it. I added a few details to the "Description" column.

\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{array}
\newcolumntype{L}{>{\centering\arraybackslash}m{3cm}}
\begin{document}
\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{|L|p{5cm}|}
\hline
\multicolumn{2}{|c|}{Request your secretary's cheeky photo collection.} \\
\hline
Step & Description \\
\hline
1 & First, ask your secretary to smile and make a funny face. \\
\hline
2 & Then, ask her to stick out her tongue. \\
\hline
3 & Finally, ask her to show off her feet. \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{center}
\end{document}


I defined a new column type L which is a centered m-column. I used the array package to define it.

I also added some text to the "Description" column to make it more complete and clear.

You can adjust the width of the "Description" column by changing the value in the p{5cm} argument.

I hope this helps!

